cig-orchestrator 1.14.0: every language in the project, one chain, no glue script.

  cigo adopt [--write] [--force] [--depth=N]
                              find every language, task runner and script folder here;
                              propose cig-tasks.json
  cigo list [--all]           components, stage groups and tasks
  cigo run <task>... [--only] [--force] [--strict] [--box|--no-box] [--versions=ask|always|never|off] [-- <args for the last task named>]
                              `cigo run test` tests every language, `cigo run ci` does
                              format-check, lint, check, build and test everywhere
  cigo plan [<task>...] [--only]
                              the order a run would take
  cigo show <task>            where a task comes from and everything it will do
  cigo audit [<task>...] [--json|--sarif|--markdown] [--offline]
                              what the guard reads before a task runs: install hooks, findings, and
                              the lockfiles' packages against OSV (name@version alone is sent)
  cigo audit --update-db [<ecosystem>...]
                              build the offline OSV database (npm, PyPI, crates.io, Go, RubyGems, Packagist, Maven, NuGet)
  cigo rehearse <npm:name[@version]|pypi:name[==version]|crates:name[@version]|./script.sh> [--json] [--keep]
                              install it in cig's contained box (Linux) and say what it did beyond its footprint
  cigo rehearse --changed [--base=<rev>] [--list] [--max=N] [--fresh] [--json|--sarif|--markdown]
                              every package the lockfiles add or change since the default branch, rehearsed
  cigo blacklist [list | add <thing> [--reason=...] [--expires=90d] | remove <entry> | why <thing> | reload]
  cigo quarantine [list | show <sha256> | clear [--all]]   what run-url downloaded, kept to read again
                              your own blacklist: packages, files, domains, ranges and URLs the guard refuses
  cigo guard [setup | scope <1-5> [--yes] | pause [30m] | off | on | allow <program> | log | uninstall [--yes]]
                              how much of this machine the guard covers: level 2 puts every package
                              manager behind it (npm install, pip install, cargo build, npx...) anywhere
  cigo undo last              undo the newest guarded call (cig unburn)
  cigo agent [run -- <command> | log | undo --session=<id>|--since=2h [--yes]]
                              what your AI agents run: boxed, read first, a person approves the risky ones
  cigo approve <id>           approve one agent command rated high (outside the agent's session)
  cigo run-url <url> [--trust] [-- <args>]
                              the safe way to curl | sh: downloaded, read, rehearsed in the box, then run
  cigo trust [<task>|list|show <task>|revoke <task>|revoke --all]
                              approve a task as it is now (signed with the tin's key), or see and drop approvals
  cigo check [--strict]       the manifest, checked before anything runs
  cigo doctor [--strict]      each toolchain: installed, which version, against the project's pins
  cigo versions [switch|keep|install [--yes]]
                              each language's pin against this machine, and whether tasks run on
                              the pinned version through mise, asdf, rustup, uv, fnm... (never your default)
  cigo outputs [<task>...]    what the last run's tasks handed on
  cigo toolchains [<name>] [--markdown]
                              the toolchains this knows
  cigo version [--json]       this cigo and the cig it runs on
  cigo update [--check] [--to=X.Y.Z]
                              install the newest release, checksum and attestation verified
  cigo crash [list|show|send|delete <id>]
                              cigo's own crash reports; sent through cig's ashtray when cig's `reports` setting says so
  cigo report <run> [--send]  a run's bundle (cig's report, the manifest's shape) for an issue; --send files it through cig
  cigo config [<key> [<value>|--unset]]
                              every setting through its layers (cigo config explain <key>)

Every command that opens a project says where versions disagree: the installed cig against
the project's pins (.cig-version, the manifest's `cig`, a script's `# cig` header) and each
toolchain against its pins (.nvmrc, go.mod...). `--strict` on check and run stops on one; `cigo versions`
runs tasks on the pinned versions through a version manager already here, per task, never your default.
Stages: setup, format, format-check, lint, check, build, test, package, run, clean.
cig's own flags go before the command: `cigo --dry-run run ci`, `cigo --no-rollback run build`.
Afterwards: `cig runs` lists every run, `cig unburn <run>` undoes one.
